00:35:19,520 --> 00:35:21,120
Bye, pal.

769
00:35:21,120 --> 00:35:22,443
(Man screams)

770
00:35:22,443 --> 00:35:23,605
- I'll tell you!

771
00:35:23,605 --> 00:35:26,550
- My mustache makes me fall sideways!

772
00:35:26,550 --> 00:35:30,155
- It's in a mansion,
I swear, in a mansion.

773
00:35:30,155 --> 00:35:31,893
But I don't know where.

774
00:35:31,893 --> 00:35:34,868
No one who's ever been there remembers it.

775
00:35:34,868 --> 00:35:36,331
Really.

776
00:35:36,331 --> 00:35:38,143
Everyone who goes there doesn't talk.

777
00:35:38,143 --> 00:35:40,223
- So no one who doesn't
go there doesn't not talk?

778
00:35:40,223 --> 00:35:42,709
- They can't remember anything.

779
00:35:42,709 --> 00:35:46,261
They can't remember anything, I swear.

780
00:35:46,261 --> 00:35:47,700
I swear.

781
00:35:47,700 --> 00:35:52,234
- Would you stop holding me by my nipples?

782
00:35:53,761 --> 00:35:56,586
- What are you doing?

783
00:35:56,586 --> 00:35:58,869
Don't leave me hanging here!

784
00:35:58,869 --> 00:35:59,744
- Tell me who shot JR?

785
00:35:59,744 --> 00:36:01,791
Come on!

786
00:36:01,791 --> 00:36:03,231
- Come back!

787
00:36:03,231 --> 00:36:05,279
- Ow, the gods are snuggying me!

788
00:36:05,279 --> 00:36:09,315
- Dorf on rituals.

789
00:36:09,315 --> 00:36:10,521
(squelching noise)

790
00:36:10,521 --> 00:36:13,752
He lands in a cow flop with this--?

791
00:36:13,752 --> 00:36:14,981
- They protected you.

792
00:36:14,981 --> 00:36:16,026
- Yeah.

793
00:36:16,026 --> 00:36:19,067
It didn't help me find out
where Kobras is hiding the mask.

794
00:36:19,067 --> 00:36:21,295
It's in a mansion, that's
all I could find out.

795
00:36:21,295 --> 00:36:22,341
- Find.

796
00:36:22,341 --> 00:36:23,685
- What do you mean, find?

797
00:36:23,685 --> 00:36:25,306
You know how many mansions
there are in London?

798
00:36:25,306 --> 00:36:26,352
- Probably like a billion!

799
00:36:26,352 --> 00:36:28,910
- I said "find" and you can find it.

800
00:36:28,910 --> 00:36:31,141
You must learn new powers.

801
00:36:31,141 --> 00:36:32,836
All you do is concentrate.

802
00:36:32,836 --> 00:36:33,828
- Here?

803
00:36:33,828 --> 00:36:36,291
- No, we go home.

804
00:36:36,291 --> 00:36:37,380
- So they can get us?

805
00:36:37,380 --> 00:36:38,949
They'll be waiting there for me.

806
00:36:38,949 --> 00:36:41,828
They're probably worrying
right now because I'm late,

807
00:36:41,828 --> 00:36:43,503
afraid something happened to me.

808
00:36:43,503 --> 00:36:45,540
- Are pumas also known for their whining?

809
00:36:45,540 --> 00:36:47,033
- Follow me.

810
00:36:47,033 --> 00:36:49,423
- I'm gonna kill you over here.

811
00:36:49,423 --> 00:36:53,932
- Pumaman--Liberace with Dockers.

812
00:36:53,932 --> 00:36:58,932
- ♫ Pumaman, when will he find love?

813
00:36:59,457 --> 00:37:02,251
♫ Pumaman♫

814
00:37:02,251 --> 00:37:04,108
(mellow music)

815
00:37:04,108 --> 00:37:05,644
- Look, you call it corn, I call it maize,

816
00:37:05,644 --> 00:37:10,644
we'll never get along.

817
00:37:11,605 --> 00:37:16,605
- That's where I almost lost
my virginity, over there.

818
00:37:19,103 --> 00:37:22,773
- High Plains Weenie.

819
00:37:22,773 --> 00:37:24,234
- What's this supposed to be?

820
00:37:24,234 --> 00:37:26,229
- My refuge.

821
00:37:26,229 --> 00:37:27,252
- It fits your proportions.

822
00:37:27,252 --> 00:37:29,781
- Do you have a small,
whiny warehouse for me?

823
00:37:29,781 --> 00:37:30,825
- If this where you sleep?

824
00:37:30,825 --> 00:37:32,798
- Why don't you kill a
pig here, what is this?

825
00:37:32,798 --> 00:37:34,056
- How do you sleep on that?

826
00:37:34,056 --> 00:37:35,477
- Are you poor, ooh?

827
00:37:35,477 --> 00:37:38,517
- How one sleeps does not matter.

828
00:37:38,517 --> 00:37:41,343
How one wakes up is important.

829
00:37:41,343 --> 00:37:42,389
Kneel!

830
00:37:42,389 --> 00:37:43,744
- Uh, the name's Tony, actually.

831
00:37:43,744 --> 00:37:46,016
- Are you sure they're out
there listening to you?

832
00:37:46,016 --> 00:37:47,412
- Of course.

833
00:37:47,412 --> 00:37:48,991
- And are they powerful?

834
00:37:48,991 --> 00:37:50,335
- Absolutely.

835
00:37:50,335 --> 00:37:52,703
- Then why don't they give us a hand?

836
00:37:52,703 --> 00:37:54,463
- They always do.

837
00:37:54,463 --> 00:37:57,322
Although we do not usually know it.

838
00:37:57,322 --> 00:37:59,294
You know it now.

839
00:37:59,294 --> 00:38:00,360
Kneel!

840
00:38:00,360 --> 00:38:05,360
- Oh, no, Tony, remember, I to--oh, oh.

841
00:38:05,427 --> 00:38:08,349
- Make silence in you.

842
00:38:08,349 --> 00:38:10,696
Leave all material things behind.

843
00:38:10,696 --> 00:38:12,275
- All my fabric?

844
00:38:12,275 --> 00:38:13,757
- Become part of the cosmos.

845
00:38:13,757 --> 00:38:15,624
- (Imitates Carl Sagan) Billions
and billions of Pumamen.

846
00:38:15,624 --> 00:38:20,008
- Concentrate your mind on
the image of the god Puma.

847
00:38:20,008 --> 00:38:22,023
Have you done this, brother?

848
00:38:22,023 --> 00:38:23,240
- I'm sorry, I wasn't listening.

849
00:38:23,240 --> 00:38:24,254
- Yes.

850
00:38:24,254 --> 00:38:26,300
- Good.

851
00:38:26,300 --> 00:38:30,248
Now think hard of that mansion.

852
00:38:30,248 --> 00:38:32,753
Concentrate.

853
00:38:32,753 --> 00:38:34,033
You will find it.

854
00:38:34,033 --> 00:38:35,889
- I can't get the "Pina
Colada" song out of my head.

855
00:38:35,889 --> 00:38:38,279
- And now prepare.

856
00:38:38,279 --> 00:38:40,369
You must take the great trip.

857
00:38:40,369 --> 00:38:41,596
- We're going to Grandma's?

858
00:38:41,596 --> 00:38:43,366
- Dive into the nothingness.

859
00:38:43,366 --> 00:38:45,522
- Watch MTV?

860
00:38:45,522 --> 00:38:50,215
- Return to the surface
where the sacred mask is.

861
00:38:50,215 --> 00:38:52,049
- How is that possible?

862
00:38:52,049 --> 00:38:54,374
- Everything is possible for the mind.

863
00:38:54,374 --> 00:38:55,483
- Well, most minds.

864
00:38:55,483 --> 00:38:57,180
- Concentrate.

865
00:38:57,180 --> 00:39:01,541
You must have faith in
your powers, in your heart.

866
00:39:01,541 --> 00:39:03,174
- In your ropy little arms.

867
00:39:03,174 --> 00:39:08,174
- If you want to, you will travel.

868
00:39:08,282 --> 00:39:10,928
Go!

869
00:39:10,928 --> 00:39:12,165
(Farms breathes deeply)

870
00:39:12,165 --> 00:39:17,165
- No, no, not that kind of go!

871
00:39:18,821 --> 00:39:22,958
- Prepare the effeminate-mobile!

872
00:39:22,958 --> 00:39:27,958
(theme music)

873
00:39:29,739 --> 00:39:31,436
- Yes.
- Yes.

874
00:39:31,436 --> 00:39:32,129
- Hi, guys!

875
00:39:32,129 --> 00:39:34,358
- You are the one, the
gods have picked you!

876
00:39:34,358 --> 00:39:36,608
- You are Coatimundi-Man.

877
00:39:36,608 --> 00:39:38,859
- And it is time to don
your hero's costume.

878
00:39:38,859 --> 00:39:40,673
Your Coatimundi look will inspire fear

879
00:39:40,673 --> 00:39:42,858
in the superstitious criminal mind.

880
00:39:42,858 --> 00:39:44,406
- Okay, well, I'll give
it a whirl, you know,

881
00:39:44,406 --> 00:39:45,482
if I've been chosen and all.

882
00:39:45,482 --> 00:39:46,475
- Evil beware!

883
00:39:46,475 --> 00:39:49,685
Coatimundi-man is born this day!

884
00:39:49,685 --> 00:39:51,210
- Okay, I'll just put on my stuff.

885
00:39:51,210 --> 00:39:54,187
I've got kind of a Rhoda vest going here.

886
00:39:54,187 --> 00:39:57,615
And, ohh, a Dr. Who scarf.

887
00:39:57,615 --> 00:39:58,777
- Yes, and with all the attendant powers

888
00:39:58,777 --> 00:40:00,516
of this majestic Coatimundi.

889
00:40:00,516 --> 00:40:02,660
For instance, um--

890
00:40:02,660 --> 00:40:04,677
- Yeah, yeah, for example, uh--

891
00:40:04,677 --> 00:40:09,677
- Well, you can shoot magnetic
laser beams from your--

892
00:40:10,554 --> 00:40:11,481
From your nose!

893
00:40:11,481 --> 00:40:12,591
- Yes, yes!

894
00:40:12,591 --> 00:40:16,004
And now he is the mighty,
yet mysterious Coatimundi.

895
00:40:16,004 --> 00:40:19,951
- His powers are yours,
it is your destiny.

896
00:40:19,951 --> 00:40:22,627
- Okay, well, you know
what, destiny or not,

897
00:40:22,627 --> 00:40:24,014
you guys, I really had my heart set

898
00:40:24,014 --> 00:40:25,709
on those cold leftover sesame noodles,

899
00:40:25,709 --> 00:40:27,918
so I'll be your mythical hero later.

900
00:40:27,918 --> 00:40:29,474
(simple children's music)

901
00:40:29,474 --> 00:40:30,382
- Wait, don't you hear?

902
00:40:30,382 --> 00:40:32,984
Your inspiring hero's
theme song is playing.

903
00:40:32,984 --> 00:40:34,327
(ratchet sounds)

904
00:40:34,327 --> 00:40:36,248
Oh, and see, the gods
are coming from space

905
00:40:36,248 --> 00:40:39,459
to tell you you must serve
or evil will triumph!

906
00:40:39,459 --> 00:40:41,964
- Wow, I see a beach ball and a string,

907
00:40:41,964 --> 00:40:42,936
and a sting and a pulley.

908
00:40:42,936 --> 00:40:44,547
And there's Gypsy, hey, Gypsy!

909
00:40:44,547 --> 00:40:45,676
- [Gypsy] Hey, Mike, sorry.

910
00:40:45,676 --> 00:40:47,256
- That's all right.

911
00:40:47,256 --> 00:40:48,133
- She's doing the will of the gods!

912
00:40:48,133 --> 00:40:49,850
- Pay no attention to her.

913
00:40:49,850 --> 00:40:50,661
- Well, you know what?

914
00:40:50,661 --> 00:40:52,419
Hey, Gypsy, I really am
gonna grab those noodles,

915
00:40:52,419 --> 00:40:53,657
you wanna split them with me?

916
00:40:53,657 --> 00:40:54,650
- [Gypsy] Yummy, let's go!

917
00:40:54,650 --> 00:40:56,398
- Ow!

918
00:40:56,398 --> 00:40:57,956
- There goes our gods.

919
00:40:57,956 --> 00:41:01,156
- Well, it would appear
that he is not yet ready

920
00:41:01,156 --> 00:41:02,991
to accept his coatimundi nature.

921
00:41:02,991 --> 00:41:05,496
- Yes, and the gods are certainly, uh--

922
00:41:05,496 --> 00:41:07,885
I think gods will be--

923
00:41:07,885 --> 00:41:10,211
Man, they're gonna finish
all the cold sesame noodles!

924
00:41:10,211 --> 00:41:11,577
(alarm sounds)

925
00:41:11,577 --> 00:41:12,813
- Let's go, let's go!

926
00:41:12,813 --> 00:41:15,160
- We're not gonna get any!

927
00:41:15,160 --> 00:41:20,160
(doors clanging)

928
00:41:25,837 --> 00:41:27,437
- You ate all the sesame
noodles, didn't you?

929
00:41:27,437 --> 00:41:30,156
- Yeah, they're all gone.

930
00:41:30,156 --> 00:41:31,458
- Help me, father!

931
00:41:31,458 --> 00:41:36,289
- My homework is really hard!

932
00:41:36,289 --> 00:41:41,289
- Excuse me, coming through.

933
00:41:41,330 --> 00:41:42,833
- Help me, father!

934
00:41:42,833 --> 00:41:45,277
- I need a couple of bucks to make rent.

935
00:41:45,277 --> 00:41:46,562
- Help me, Vadinho!

936
00:41:46,562 --> 00:41:51,562
♫ Help me, Vadinho,
help, help me Vadinho ♫

937
00:41:53,603 --> 00:41:55,137
(Sniffs) They have cats!

938
00:41:55,137 --> 00:41:56,781
Oh, no, that's me.

939
00:41:56,781 --> 00:41:58,754
- Would you take that off?

940
00:41:58,754 --> 00:42:00,385
- Look, just don't use
the holodeck any more

941
00:42:00,385 --> 00:42:04,642
if you don't know how to use it.

942
00:42:04,642 --> 00:42:05,494
- (sighs) Thank you.

943
00:42:05,494 --> 00:42:08,119
- Guy who lives on the second floor.

944
00:42:08,119 --> 00:42:10,212
- You're pretty.

945
00:42:10,212 --> 00:42:12,464
- Did you find it?

946
00:42:12,464 --> 00:42:13,488
- No.

947
00:42:13,488 --> 00:42:15,248
- What are you doing, I
thought you were gonna find it.

948
00:42:15,248 --> 00:42:17,081
It's okay, I just, I thought
you were gonna find it.

949
00:42:17,081 --> 00:42:19,034
- I learned that I can only
project myself to a place

950
00:42:19,034 --> 00:42:21,006
that I know.

951
00:42:21,006 --> 00:42:23,428
I have to know exactly where I wanna go

952
00:42:23,428 --> 00:42:25,402
otherwise I'll get lost into nothingness.

953
00:42:25,402 --> 00:42:26,691
- So it's off to Hooter's.

954
00:42:26,691 --> 00:42:27,972
- Then we are no closer.

955
00:42:27,972 --> 00:42:29,763
- So you whizzed it.

956
00:42:29,763 --> 00:42:30,895
- Listen, Vadinho--

957
00:42:30,895 --> 00:42:33,775
- Are you a kind of onion?

958
00:42:33,775 --> 00:42:35,247
- Is finding the mask the only way?

959
00:42:35,247 --> 00:42:40,247
- Yes. If we do not succeed
terrible things will happen.

960
00:42:40,376 --> 00:42:42,275
- The gods will give you the wet look.

961
00:42:42,275 --> 00:42:43,854
- They have lost their connection.

962
00:42:43,854 --> 00:42:45,710
- The network is down.

963
00:42:45,710 --> 00:42:47,875
- The mask is serving evil.

964
00:42:47,875 --> 00:42:50,584
- Can't they do anything from up there?

965
00:42:50,584 --> 00:42:53,518
- Man is free, man is master of himself.

966
00:42:53,518 --> 00:42:54,861
- Man sounds cool.

967
00:42:54,861 --> 00:42:57,880
- But if they come, man is no longer free.

968
00:42:57,880 --> 00:42:59,992
- Man could get pricy.

969
00:42:59,992 --> 00:43:01,965
- You must concentrate.

970
00:43:01,965 --> 00:43:03,981
You will find the solution in your mind.

971
00:43:03,981 --> 00:43:05,677
- I think we saw the limits of his mind

972
00:43:05,677 --> 00:43:08,769
just a few minutes ago.

973
00:43:08,769 --> 00:43:11,893
- Let's not be roommates any more, okay?

974
00:43:11,893 --> 00:43:13,743
(upbeat music)

975
00:43:13,743 --> 00:43:18,743
- I'm thinking of having
my chin smallened.

976
00:43:19,332 --> 00:43:20,590
- (Tom imitating Gilbert
Gottfried) I'm in the firetruck

977
00:43:20,590 --> 00:43:23,856
for USA Up All Night.

978
00:43:23,856 --> 00:43:28,856
- Soundtrack by my little brother's Casio.

979
00:43:29,104 --> 00:43:32,634
- I keep dreaming of a
little man in a tiny tower.

980
00:43:32,634 --> 00:43:35,727
- Uh, hi.

981
00:43:35,727 --> 00:43:38,283
- Where did you come from?
- Out there.

982
00:43:38,336 --> 00:43:39,779
- What sort of a story's that?

983
00:43:39,779 --> 00:43:41,088
- I'm the Pumaman.

984
00:43:41,088 --> 00:43:42,464
- I mean, who is this guy?

985
00:43:42,464 --> 00:43:43,351
- Who's he, somebody out of a comic strip?

986
00:43:43,351 --> 00:43:44,319
I've never heard of him.

987
00:43:44,319 --> 00:43:46,472
- He didn't materialize until yesterday.

988
00:43:46,472 --> 00:43:47,815
- Well, are you getting
anything out of it?

989
00:43:47,815 --> 00:43:49,608
- Mostly trouble.

990
00:43:49,608 --> 00:43:51,027
- I told you Tony, if you want adventure

991
00:43:51,027 --> 00:43:52,371
why don't you join up with us?

992
00:43:52,371 --> 00:43:53,340
It's all the sports you can take,

993
00:43:53,340 --> 00:43:55,623
high jump, low jump, you get
a free sauna at the end of it.

994
00:43:55,623 --> 00:43:57,426
- I'll keep that in mind, Martin.

995
00:43:57,426 --> 00:43:59,217
But in the meantime, you
wouldn't happen to have

996
00:43:59,217 --> 00:44:01,608
a transmitter and receiver
to lend me, would you?

997
00:44:01,608 --> 00:44:03,463
- You mean a position indicator?

998
00:44:03,463 --> 00:44:04,285
- Yeah.

999
00:44:04,285 --> 00:44:07,229
- Hey, an old donut back here.

1000
00:44:07,229 --> 00:44:09,318
- Here's the pacemaker, thanks
for letting me borrow it.

1001
00:44:09,318 --> 00:44:12,828
(indicator beeps)

1002
00:44:12,828 --> 00:44:14,033
- How does it work?

1003
00:44:14,033 --> 00:44:16,326
- The closer you get, the
more constant the bleep.

1004
00:44:16,326 --> 00:44:17,659
- Over what range?

1005
00:44:17,659 --> 00:44:19,771
- Up to two miles.

1006
00:44:19,771 --> 00:44:22,321
- Okay, and if you slow
down, I'll get out.

1007
00:44:22,321 --> 00:44:23,206
- You mean here?

1008
00:44:23,206 --> 00:44:25,553
- No, I'm going the other way.

1009
00:44:25,553 --> 00:44:26,501
- What did you say you do?

1010
00:44:26,501 --> 00:44:27,408
The Sandwich-man?

1011
00:44:27,408 --> 00:44:30,917
- No, the Pumaman, that's
a whole different bag.

1012
00:44:30,917 --> 00:44:32,208
- What are you advertising?

1013
00:44:32,208 --> 00:44:35,279
- Men from outer space.

1014
00:44:35,279 --> 00:44:35,877
- He is the Pumaman!

1015
00:44:35,877 --> 00:44:39,735
He can get out of a car
going three miles an hour.

1016
00:44:39,735 --> 00:44:40,485
(door slams)

1017
00:44:40,485 --> 00:44:42,000
- The Queen!

1018
00:44:42,000 --> 00:44:44,909
(crash)

1019
00:44:44,909 --> 00:44:47,013
- (laughs) A steering column
plunged through his chest,

1020
00:44:47,013 --> 00:44:48,667
that's great.

1021
00:44:48,667 --> 00:44:52,912
- (British accent) Lost control
of me bladder, sorry, mate!

1022
00:44:52,912 --> 00:44:55,895
- You have the jaws of life on you?

1023
00:44:55,895 --> 00:44:57,367
- (laughs)

1024
00:44:57,367 --> 00:45:01,957
- I've a good mind to join
a marching band, you--

1025
00:45:03,510 --> 00:45:08,510
- Oh, where am I gonna get
another personal fire truck?

1026
00:45:13,099 --> 00:45:18,099
- Oh, I did deserve all
those beatings as a child.

1027
00:45:21,153 --> 00:45:22,533
(arrow twanging)

1028
00:45:22,533 --> 00:45:23,578
- Cupid!

1029
00:45:23,578 --> 00:45:27,940
(tense music)

1030
00:45:27,940 --> 00:45:28,790
- Here he comes.

1031
00:45:28,790 --> 00:45:32,104
- Light the candles!

1032
00:45:32,108 --> 00:45:35,819
- Trying to net some tuna
and we got this thing.

1033
00:45:35,819 --> 00:45:37,302
- Call him.

1034
00:45:37,302 --> 00:45:42,155
- He's playing with mommy's lipstick.

1035
00:45:42,155 --> 00:45:43,904
- Don't come in, Tony, run!

1036
00:45:43,904 --> 00:45:46,037
- Eat this baguette, eat it!

1037
00:45:46,037 --> 00:45:49,216
(Vadinho screams in pain)

1038
00:45:49,216 --> 00:45:51,318
(Tom growls)

1039
00:45:51,318 --> 00:45:55,534
- The Pyoo-may-man.

1040
00:45:58,022 --> 00:45:59,292
- More ketchup please.

1041
00:45:59,292 --> 00:46:02,414
- Don't worry about me, watch out!

1042
00:46:02,414 --> 00:46:06,497
- He used his trolling motor on them.

1043
00:46:06,497 --> 00:46:11,497
- Ooh, I think he officially bonked them.

1044
00:46:12,336 --> 00:46:16,582
- Beat me, fine, but to drape a net on me?

1045
00:46:16,582 --> 00:46:17,883
- (whines) And then they snagged on me

1046
00:46:17,883 --> 00:46:18,950
and called me "Prince Valiant" and said

1047
00:46:18,950 --> 00:46:23,950
I had a stupid fakey religion.

1048
00:46:25,894 --> 00:46:28,870
- Don't let them net me.

1049
00:46:28,870 --> 00:46:32,283
- Save yourself, disappear.

1050
00:46:32,283 --> 00:46:33,976
Please do it.

1051
00:46:33,976 --> 00:46:35,060
(funky music)

1052
00:46:35,060 --> 00:46:37,524
- Do the Hustle!

1053
00:46:37,524 --> 00:46:40,405
- Score, it's good.

1054
00:46:40,405 --> 00:46:45,405
- Into this piece of drywall.

1055
00:46:48,810 --> 00:46:51,337
- Just doing his floor routine.

1056
00:46:51,337 --> 00:46:52,298
- There he is!

1057
00:46:52,298 --> 00:46:53,503
(gunfire)

1058
00:46:53,503 --> 00:46:57,567
- Ow, ow, ow, I'm dead, okay, ow, ow!

1059
00:46:57,567 --> 00:46:58,911
- Molasses!

1060
00:46:58,911 --> 00:47:02,206
- I don't see him any
more, (inaudible) anyway.

1061
00:47:02,206 --> 00:47:03,603
- I don't think he knows
these guys are here.

1062
00:47:03,603 --> 00:47:05,738
He's just playing around them.

1063
00:47:05,738 --> 00:47:06,719
(gunfire)

1064
00:47:06,719 --> 00:47:10,453
- Whee, this is fun!

1065
00:47:10,453 --> 00:47:12,311
- I love the Pyoo-may-man.

1066
00:47:12,311 --> 00:47:14,113
- (inaudible) Shoot!

1067
00:47:14,113 --> 00:47:15,533
- Yeah, in ten to twelve hours they should

1068
00:47:15,533 --> 00:47:18,813
be out of ammo.

1069
00:47:18,813 --> 00:47:21,086
- My kapok!

1070
00:47:21,086 --> 00:47:25,150
(gunfire)

1071
00:47:25,150 --> 00:47:27,687
- I just wanna check your axle here.

1072
00:47:27,687 --> 00:47:29,427
- Brake, step on the brakes!

1073
00:47:29,427 --> 00:47:31,911
(Men screaming)

1074
00:47:31,911 --> 00:47:36,471
- So this lousy movie ruins
a perfectly good Jaguar.

1075
00:47:36,696 --> 00:47:40,151
- Hey, what's going on?

1076
00:47:40,151 --> 00:47:44,423
- The Archangel Duane.

1077
00:47:44,423 --> 00:47:47,633
- Tony, you have power in your hands!

1078
00:47:47,633 --> 00:47:49,533
Your hands are claws!

1079
00:47:49,533 --> 00:47:51,718
- Sorry I forgot to tell you about that.

1080
00:47:51,718 --> 00:47:55,782
- Pumaman can rip through
pure Contact Paper.

1081
00:47:55,782 --> 00:47:59,495
(Men shouting)

1082
00:47:59,495 --> 00:48:01,659
- I am joining your carpool!

1083
00:48:01,659 --> 00:48:03,218
- These poor guys aren't
even the villains.

1084
00:48:03,218 --> 00:48:04,262
They just came to get some stuff

1085
00:48:04,262 --> 00:48:07,024
out of their U-Stor-It.

1086
00:48:07,024 --> 00:48:12,024
- Well, time to drop in on
the Super Bowl at half-time.

1087
00:48:12,710 --> 00:48:15,792
- Meanwhile, in Georgy Girl--

1088
00:48:15,792 --> 00:48:20,346
- She's driving the cameraman to school.

1089
00:48:20,346 --> 00:48:21,495
- Snoopy.

1090
00:48:21,495 --> 00:48:23,058
(spring boings)

1091
00:48:23,058 --> 00:48:25,148
- Now he gets drunk and pops
into old girlfriend's car.

1092
00:48:25,148 --> 00:48:26,259
- Tony, how did you get here?

1093
00:48:26,259 --> 00:48:27,421
- Never mind, drive.

1094
00:48:27,421 --> 00:48:28,445
- He said.

1095
00:48:28,445 --> 00:48:30,067
- But they'll kill you if they find you.

1096
00:48:30,067 --> 00:48:31,805
Kobras wants to kill you.

1097
00:48:31,805 --> 00:48:33,480
They're following me,
they're right behind me.

1098
00:48:33,480 --> 00:48:35,292
- Never mind, tell me where the mask is.

1099
00:48:35,292 --> 00:48:36,658
- Get your copy at Blockbuster's.

1100
00:48:36,658 --> 00:48:38,311
- Don't ask me that.

1101
00:48:38,311 --> 00:48:40,261
I can't.

1102
00:48:40,261 --> 00:48:42,885
I swear I'd like to, but I can't.

1103
00:48:42,885 --> 00:48:45,551
I'm conditioned to keep the
secret, just like everyone.

1104
00:48:45,551 --> 00:48:47,225
I can't do it.

1105
00:48:47,225 --> 00:48:48,506
- Try! Fight him!

1106
00:48:48,506 --> 00:48:49,690
Fight him with your will!

1107
00:48:49,690 --> 00:48:51,331
- But my will won't.

1108
00:48:51,331 --> 00:48:54,147
- I-I-can't, he's commanding
me from a distance.

1109
00:48:54,147 --> 00:48:55,353
- Amelia Airhead.

1110
00:48:55,353 --> 00:48:57,209
- I can't do it.

1111
00:48:57,209 --> 00:48:58,745
Tony, help me.

1112
00:48:58,745 --> 00:49:00,324
Free me!

1113
00:49:00,324 --> 00:49:04,312
Something terrible's happening
to me and to everyone.

1114
00:49:04,312 --> 00:49:06,264
Help me, don't leave me.

1115
00:49:06,264 --> 00:49:09,602
- A helmet, or a hat, or what the--

1116
00:49:09,602 --> 00:49:11,929
- Sorry, we stopped for Slurpees.

1117
00:49:11,929 --> 00:49:13,602
- There they are, run!

1118
00:49:13,602 --> 00:49:15,415
Run! Save yourself!

1119
00:49:15,415 --> 00:49:18,040
- Play your theme music and hop around!

1120
00:49:18,040 --> 00:49:22,499
- We now revisit Brideshead
and do a revisiting.

1121
00:49:22,499 --> 00:49:27,499
- It's one of Sting's cabins.

1122
00:49:28,422 --> 00:49:33,422
- I think she's visiting
Helena Bonham Carter.

1123
00:49:34,895 --> 00:49:36,175
- Man, with those boots she has to use

1124
00:49:36,175 --> 00:49:40,790
high-altitude baking directions.

1125
00:49:40,790 --> 00:49:43,934
(interceptor beeps slowly)

1126
00:49:43,934 --> 00:49:45,469
(receiver beeps quickly)

1127
00:49:45,469 --> 00:49:47,708
- Mr. McGregor's about to shoot them.

1128
00:49:47,708 --> 00:49:49,108
(beeping quickens)

1129
00:49:49,108 --> 00:49:49,794
- Uh-oh, he's in d-fib!

1130
00:49:49,794 --> 00:49:51,142
Get the crash cart stat!

1131
00:49:51,142 --> 00:49:55,717
(constant beep)

1132
00:49:55,717 --> 00:49:59,856
- (calming voice) This is a
test of the audience's patience.

1133
00:49:59,856 --> 00:50:04,856
- Think we're gonna sell a lot of these.

1134
00:50:06,309 --> 00:50:09,370
- Hey, a raccoon.

1135
00:50:09,370 --> 00:50:14,313
- Goldfinger's riding with Octopussy.

1136
00:50:17,498 --> 00:50:21,401
- I'll go mess up and you save me.

1137
00:50:21,401 --> 00:50:22,959
- Meet me in the laboratory.

1138
00:50:22,959 --> 00:50:26,301
- And don't ever out-dress me again.

1139
00:50:26,301 --> 00:50:30,685
- I don't believe you
guys mooned us back there.

1140
00:50:30,685 --> 00:50:31,591
- It's confirmed.

1141
00:50:31,591 --> 00:50:35,945
They brought a Bundt cake.

1142
00:50:35,945 --> 00:50:37,940
- High-ranking officers.

1143
00:50:37,940 --> 00:50:39,273
What the hell are they doing here?

1144
00:50:39,273 --> 00:50:41,506
- Book club.

1145
00:50:41,506 --> 00:50:42,727
(footsteps)

1146
00:50:42,727 --> 00:50:45,745
- Ah, my posse.

1147
00:50:45,745 --> 00:50:49,253
- Let the cookie exchange begin.

1148
00:50:49,253 --> 00:50:54,253
- Hey, wait, I don't want
to sit next to Pinochet.

1149
00:50:54,522 --> 00:50:56,422
- A couple of dictators
brought dictator friends

1150
00:50:56,422 --> 00:51:00,379
so they had to put in the leaf.

1151
00:51:00,379 --> 00:51:02,971
- Time to plan the NATO picnic.

1152
00:51:02,971 --> 00:51:06,523
- Gentlemen, I'm so glad
that you considered my house

1153
00:51:06,523 --> 00:51:09,776
a suitable place for this summit meeting.

1154
00:51:09,776 --> 00:51:11,056
- Though I wish you'd told me.

1155
00:51:11,056 --> 00:51:15,119
- I'm going to leave you
now to make your decision.

1156
00:51:15,119 --> 00:51:18,181
- Who want's what on your pizza?

1157
00:51:18,181 --> 00:51:19,365
- Do you believe what he's wearing?

1158
00:51:19,365 --> 00:51:22,830
(stage whispers)

1159
00:51:22,830 --> 00:51:27,310
- Hope you brought swim
trunks, heh, heh, heh.

1160
00:51:27,310 --> 00:51:28,734
(door slams)

1161
00:51:28,734 --> 00:51:31,394
- [Man] Seems strange that we
don't know anything about him.

1162
00:51:31,394 --> 00:51:32,792
He's not in our file.

1163
00:51:32,792 --> 00:51:35,255
- Quite. Besides being a charming host

1164
00:51:35,255 --> 00:51:38,061
what credentials can
this Mr. Kobras offer us?

1165
00:51:38,061 --> 00:51:40,332
He's unknown to our services as well.

1166
00:51:40,332 --> 00:51:42,988
- That means he's not compromised.

1167
00:51:42,988 --> 00:51:44,139
- No one else wore a cape.

1168
00:51:44,139 --> 00:51:46,481
- He managed to elude our security,

1169
00:51:46,481 --> 00:51:48,466
which means he's so smart he can do it.

1170
00:51:48,466 --> 00:51:50,738
- That's a distorted way of reasoning.

1171
00:51:50,738 --> 00:51:53,543
- Is it distorted to ask
why this summit meeting

1172
00:51:53,543 --> 00:51:55,911
of the heads of state
of the entire world--

1173
00:51:55,911 --> 00:51:57,234
- (Imitates Inspector
Clouseau) My minky is here.

1174
00:51:57,234 --> 00:51:58,534
- Must be held on private property?

1175
00:51:58,534 --> 00:52:00,071
- It's customary to hold
this kind of meeting in

1176
00:52:00,071 --> 00:52:02,480
reserved and selected locations.

1177
00:52:02,480 --> 00:52:04,348
Everything becomes less formal.

1178
00:52:04,348 --> 00:52:06,128
It's not the first time.

1179
00:52:06,128 --> 00:52:10,267
- But does this mansion
offer sufficient guarantees?

1180
00:52:10,267 --> 00:52:14,374
- It's so great that they
wanna see my cabaret act.

1181
00:52:14,374 --> 00:52:18,971
- I better get my wiener
wraps out of the oven.

1182
00:52:18,971 --> 00:52:23,035
- She does her roots
black for some reason.

1183
00:52:23,035 --> 00:52:25,381
(bell sounds, mechanical noise)

1184
00:52:25,381 --> 00:52:27,002
- Wienie.

1185
00:52:27,002 --> 00:52:28,378
- They used to have a
carny running that ride,

1186
00:52:28,378 --> 00:52:31,833
but the salary got too much.

1187
00:52:31,833 --> 00:52:33,317
(noise stops)

1188
00:52:33,317 --> 00:52:38,317
- This will take a little bit,
I'm still installing Windows.

1189
00:52:40,355 --> 00:52:41,775
- Do you guys like North Korea?

1190
00:52:41,775 --> 00:52:44,899
I sure don't.

1191
00:52:44,899 --> 00:52:48,153
- I'll use my powers of looking.

1192
00:52:48,153 --> 00:52:53,153
- (Tom gasps) There's
another meeting over there!

1193
00:52:54,166 --> 00:52:55,862
- Goldfinger got Mike Tyson!

1194
00:52:55,862 --> 00:52:56,982
- No!

1195
00:52:56,982 --> 00:52:59,691
(strange noises)

1196
00:52:59,691 --> 00:53:02,336
- The Botany 500-man.

1197
00:53:02,336 --> 00:53:07,307
- Uh-oh, they left the
meeting on too long.

1198
00:53:07,307 --> 00:53:11,882
- Now he sees through a glass, dumbly.

1199
00:53:11,882 --> 00:53:16,882
- (deep voice) Shimmy shimmy,co-co
bop, shimmy shimmy bop.

1200
00:53:22,123 --> 00:53:26,516
- We're all agreed then,
Carrot-top is the best comic.

1201
00:53:26,516 --> 00:53:31,114
- Yes, much better than Yahoo Serious.

1202
00:53:31,114 --> 00:53:32,063
- Are they trying to resell this

1203
00:53:32,063 --> 00:53:33,385
as a Hallmark Christmas Special,

1204
00:53:33,385 --> 00:53:37,365
one that didn't get a
theatrical release, you know?

1205
00:53:41,955 --> 00:53:45,764
- (Sighs) Well, I'm just
gonna go get our water.

1206
00:53:45,764 --> 00:53:47,342
- Fine, gentlemen.

1207
00:53:47,342 --> 00:53:49,113
We can go home.

1208
00:53:49,113 --> 00:53:53,080
You will receive further
instructions at the proper time.

1209
00:53:53,080 --> 00:53:55,149
- This was great, we should
do it again sometime,

1210
00:53:55,149 --> 00:53:59,352
great to see you guys, let's
take the scenic road, bye.

1211
00:53:59,352 --> 00:54:01,069
(buzzing)

1212
00:54:01,069 --> 00:54:02,019
- I've run out of quarters.

1213
00:54:02,019 --> 00:54:05,313
- The men who control the destiny
of the world will be here.

1214
00:54:05,313 --> 00:54:06,593
- Barry Diller, here?

1215
00:54:06,593 --> 00:54:09,495
- When the world is
mine, I alone will decide

1216
00:54:09,495 --> 00:54:13,089
whether it is to be war
or peace, life or death.

1217
00:54:13,089 --> 00:54:14,093
- Stuffing or potatoes.

1218
00:54:14,093 --> 00:54:17,410
- According to the new order
which I shall establish.

1219
00:54:17,410 --> 00:54:20,364
- Hey, did the Plantagenets
have a burning permit?

1220
00:54:20,364 --> 00:54:23,328
- They immediately slap Molly
Hatchett in the tape deck.

1221
00:54:23,328 --> 00:54:25,559
- You will never again leave me

1222
00:54:25,559 --> 00:54:30,485
for this irrational feeling you call love.

1223
00:54:30,485 --> 00:54:33,430
I have an assignment for you.

1224
00:54:33,430 --> 00:54:35,712
Tony Farms is the Pyoo-ma-man.

1225
00:54:35,712 --> 00:54:36,501
- Poo-ma-man.

1226
00:54:36,501 --> 00:54:38,101
- The Pumaman is my enemy.

1227
00:54:38,101 --> 00:54:38,831
- Poo-ma-man.

1228
00:54:38,831 --> 00:54:41,689
- Whoever is my enemy
is your enemy as well.

1229
00:54:41,689 --> 00:54:43,940
He must die.

1230
00:54:43,940 --> 00:54:48,940
- Anyway, toes on the
line, look up a little.

1231
00:54:49,070 --> 00:54:54,070
- He must die, and you shall
be the one to kill him.

1232
00:54:54,316 --> 00:54:58,971
(strange noises)

1233
00:54:58,971 --> 00:55:02,950
When he comes looking for
you, greet him, smile at him.

1234
00:55:02,950 --> 00:55:03,803
- Buy him a beer.

1235
00:55:03,803 --> 00:55:05,594
- But you will be ready.

1236
00:55:05,594 --> 00:55:06,778
Take this gun.

1237
00:55:06,778 --> 00:55:10,672
- I've got plenty, I'll
never use it, please take it.

1238
00:55:10,672 --> 00:55:13,828
- When he comes near you, shoot him.

1239
00:55:13,828 --> 00:55:14,831
- Can I do it tomorrow?

1240
00:55:14,831 --> 00:55:16,271
I have nail wraps scheduled.

1241
00:55:16,271 --> 00:55:17,732
- Kill him!

1242
00:55:17,732 --> 00:55:18,640
Finish him off!

1243
00:55:18,640 --> 00:55:19,759
- But funny things on him!

1244
00:55:19,759 --> 00:55:21,007
Show people his butt!

1245
00:55:21,007 --> 00:55:23,279
- It will be the greatest act of love.

1246
00:55:23,279 --> 00:55:25,422
- So go to Stewart Anderson's
with him, then sleep with him,

1247
00:55:25,422 --> 00:55:28,579
got it.

1248
00:55:28,579 --> 00:55:32,430
- Is this a Glock I see before me?

1249
00:55:32,430 --> 00:55:37,423
- It will be an act of
love from you to me.

1250
00:55:37,423 --> 00:55:38,542
Do you understand me?

1251
00:55:38,542 --> 00:55:41,528
- Or am I talking to my heads, here, what?

1252
00:55:41,528 --> 00:55:46,019
- Hey, a statue of Whoopie Goldberg.

1253
00:55:46,019 --> 00:55:47,897
- Hey, Sondra Locke's gonna
take the direct approach

1254
00:55:47,897 --> 00:55:52,055
with Clint.

1255
00:55:53,574 --> 00:55:58,574
- The slack-wearing superhero.

1256
00:56:00,300 --> 00:56:05,300
- Now, careful, you're
gonna clip one of the heads.

1257
00:56:06,380 --> 00:56:09,003
(Jane cries out)

1258
00:56:09,003 --> 00:56:12,165
- ♫Love to love you, baby ♫

1259
00:56:12,165 --> 00:56:13,254
(gunshot)

1260
00:56:13,254 --> 00:56:16,038
(Tom makes Donald Duck noise)

1261
00:56:16,038 --> 00:56:17,637
(Jane cries out)

1262
00:56:17,637 --> 00:56:22,385
- I can fly two miles an hour.

1263
00:56:22,385 --> 00:56:25,584
- Tony, run!

1264
00:56:25,584 --> 00:56:30,584
- Constantly-Out-Of-His-League-Man.

1265
00:56:30,960 --> 00:56:35,578
- His fortress of Balditude.

1266
00:56:35,578 --> 00:56:39,238
- Laserium, featuring the
music of Donald Pleasence.

1267
00:56:39,238 --> 00:56:41,360
(Tony screams)

1268
00:56:41,360 --> 00:56:42,575
- He's the kind of guy
who'd stick his tongue

1269
00:56:42,575 --> 00:56:45,177
on a frozen flagpole twice.

1270
00:56:45,177 --> 00:56:46,829
(Tony screams)

1271
00:56:46,829 --> 00:56:51,555
- Yeah, he just can't
like his book pow-ell.

1272
00:56:51,555 --> 00:56:54,295
- Oh, blew a breaker, someone
must be using the toaster.

1273
00:56:54,295 --> 00:56:58,005
- Stop! Your powers
are worn out! Finished!

1274
00:56:58,005 --> 00:56:59,377
- Done! Completed!

1275
00:56:59,377 --> 00:57:04,281
- Threadbare! Shiny at the elbows!

1276
00:57:04,281 --> 00:57:06,490
- You cannot escape me, Pyoo-ma-man!

1277
00:57:06,490 --> 00:57:09,476
- POO-MA-MAN!

1278
00:57:09,476 --> 00:57:14,476
Oh, is that right, Dee-on-ald?

1279
00:57:14,639 --> 00:57:18,670
- You're just a small,
insignificant human being--

1280
00:57:18,670 --> 00:57:22,373
- That's hoo-man being, oh, no ...

1281
00:57:22,526 --> 00:57:26,590
- I'm supposed to come up with
a snappy retort and I can't.

1282
00:57:26,590 --> 00:57:29,599
- This is where the little
elevator really pays off.

1283
00:57:29,599 --> 00:57:31,522
(strange noises)

1284
00:57:31,522 --> 00:57:35,950
(theme music)

1285
00:57:37,161 --> 00:57:42,161
- Are you leaning on
the switch over there?

1286
00:57:42,269 --> 00:57:45,576
(upbeat music)

1287
00:57:45,576 --> 00:57:48,521
- The door is like two steps to the right.

1288
00:57:48,521 --> 00:57:53,521
- Man, one of those
prefab English castles.

1289
00:57:54,834 --> 00:57:56,434
- Uh, Puma, honey, if
you keep your legs up,

1290
00:57:56,434 --> 00:58:01,275
you'll go faster.

1291
00:58:01,275 --> 00:58:02,822
- Tony Farms.

1292
00:58:02,822 --> 00:58:03,921
- Raises soybeans.

1293
00:58:03,921 --> 00:58:06,609
- You must obey me.

1294
00:58:06,609 --> 00:58:08,070
