1330
01:00:28,911 --> 01:00:32,973
- First save me, then change me.

1331
01:00:32,973 --> 01:00:34,457
- Tony Farms.

1332
01:00:34,457 --> 01:00:35,246
- He has forty acres.

1333
01:00:35,246 --> 01:00:38,659
- Your body no longer belongs to you.

1334
01:00:38,659 --> 01:00:41,347
The forces of the cosmos
have turned you over to me.

1335
01:00:41,347 --> 01:00:42,261
(crunching sound)

1336
01:00:42,261 --> 01:00:44,191
- Are the heads eating potato chips?

1337
01:00:44,191 --> 01:00:46,976
- Come back to me!

1338
01:00:46,976 --> 01:00:48,533
I order you to return!

1339
01:00:48,533 --> 01:00:50,367
- Mach schnell!

1340
01:00:50,367 --> 01:00:52,128
- I am waiting for you!

1341
01:00:52,128 --> 01:00:52,731
(Tony screams)

1342
01:00:52,731 --> 01:00:54,618
- I'm back on catnip,
man, you gotta help me!

1343
01:00:54,618 --> 01:00:55,910
- Help me, Vadinho!

1344
01:00:55,910 --> 01:00:56,869
He's calling me!

1345
01:00:56,869 --> 01:00:58,309
Can you hear him, can you hear him?

1346
01:00:58,309 --> 01:00:59,653
I can't fight it!

1347
01:00:59,653 --> 01:01:01,092
- Calm yourself!

1348
01:01:01,092 --> 01:01:01,883
(Tony screams)

1349
01:01:01,883 --> 01:01:03,578
- I can't, I've got to go!

1350
01:01:03,578 --> 01:01:04,367
- Chewing the scenery.

1351
01:01:04,367 --> 01:01:05,199
- If you go, you're lost!

1352
01:01:05,199 --> 01:01:06,735
They'll kill you!

1353
01:01:06,735 --> 01:01:09,796
You must resist!

1354
01:01:09,796 --> 01:01:12,399
Repeat with me, "Each man is a god.

1355
01:01:12,399 --> 01:01:14,052
"Each man is free."

1356
01:01:14,052 --> 01:01:16,068
Do not think of anything else.

1357
01:01:16,068 --> 01:01:17,924
Concentrate!!

1358
01:01:17,924 --> 01:01:20,174
Repeat, repeat with me,

1359
01:01:20,174 --> 01:01:20,846
- - With me.

1360
01:01:20,846 --> 01:01:21,987
- Each man is a god.

1361
01:01:21,987 --> 01:01:24,152
Each man is free.

1362
01:01:24,152 --> 01:01:25,560
Each man is a god.

1363
01:01:25,560 --> 01:01:26,840
- Each man is a god.

1364
01:01:26,840 --> 01:01:28,068
- Each man is free.

1365
01:01:28,068 --> 01:01:29,625
- Each man is free.

1366
01:01:29,625 --> 01:01:30,691
- Each man is a god.

1367
01:01:30,691 --> 01:01:31,993
- Each man is a weenie.

1368
01:01:31,993 --> 01:01:33,486
- Each man is a god.

1369
01:01:33,486 --> 01:01:34,478
- Each man is free.

1370
01:01:34,478 --> 01:01:35,682
- Each man is a puss, okay.

1371
01:01:35,682 --> 01:01:37,081
- Each man is free.

1372
01:01:37,081 --> 01:01:38,147
- (cracking noise)

1373
01:01:38,147 --> 01:01:40,119
- These walnuts are good.

1374
01:01:40,119 --> 01:01:43,138
- Mr. Forbes is here if
you wanna go for a ride.

1375
01:01:43,138 --> 01:01:44,739
- I've taken away his powers.

1376
01:01:44,739 --> 01:01:46,093
- So that's done, anyway.

1377
01:01:46,093 --> 01:01:48,664
- And his will is broken.

1378
01:01:48,664 --> 01:01:51,565
But he's putting up an
unexpected resistance.

1379
01:01:51,565 --> 01:01:54,694
- I'll take care of it.

1380
01:01:54,694 --> 01:01:56,257
- Comb the area, find him!

1381
01:01:56,257 --> 01:01:58,135
And don't make any noise.

1382
01:01:58,135 --> 01:01:59,969
I don't want any trouble around here.

1383
01:01:59,969 --> 01:02:04,969
- 'Cause the police would
find out I'm pirating cable.

1384
01:02:05,195 --> 01:02:07,308
- I'll break a few more
wills before lunch,

1385
01:02:07,308 --> 01:02:09,537
then meet some (inaudible) on Friday.

1386
01:02:09,537 --> 01:02:10,583
- Pyoo-ma-man.

1387
01:02:10,583 --> 01:02:12,044
- Poo-ma-man, boy!

1388
01:02:12,044 --> 01:02:13,993
Pumaman, I am ordering you--

1389
01:02:13,993 --> 01:02:16,527
(cracking noise)

1390
01:02:16,527 --> 01:02:18,019
I am ordering you--

1391
01:02:18,019 --> 01:02:20,269
- A fajita, is that okay?

1392
01:02:20,269 --> 01:02:23,896
- To kill yourself.

1393
01:02:23,896 --> 01:02:25,581
- John-boy Walton!

1394
01:02:25,581 --> 01:02:30,253
- I like the other head better.

1395
01:02:30,253 --> 01:02:32,781
- It's all right, Vadinho.

1396
01:02:32,781 --> 01:02:33,741
It's over.

1397
01:02:33,741 --> 01:02:34,667
- Oh, great! So can we go, Mike?

1398
01:02:34,667 --> 01:02:38,095
- No.
- Damn.

1399
01:02:38,095 --> 01:02:39,382
- Listen, I want you to hear my epitaph.

1400
01:02:39,382 --> 01:02:41,376
- "I'm with stupid."

1401
01:02:41,376 --> 01:02:43,403
- He wasn't much in his
life, either as a man,

1402
01:02:43,403 --> 01:02:45,675
or a Pumaman.

1403
01:02:45,675 --> 01:02:47,371
And now he's worth absolutely nothing.

1404
01:02:47,371 --> 01:02:49,130
- The same as when he was alive.

1405
01:02:49,130 --> 01:02:50,944
- That is not true.

1406
01:02:50,944 --> 01:02:51,988
You are a worthy man.

1407
01:02:51,988 --> 01:02:53,056
- Worthy of a beating.

1408
01:02:53,056 --> 01:02:55,189
- You will be all right.

1409
01:02:55,189 --> 01:02:57,194
- Only if I lose a habit.

1410
01:02:57,194 --> 01:02:58,101
- Which one?

1411
01:02:58,101 --> 01:03:00,949
- Nose-picking? Public farting?

1412
01:03:00,949 --> 01:03:03,667
- Wanting to live!!

1413
01:03:03,667 --> 01:03:06,334
- Gotta clock these windows, quick!

1414
01:03:06,334 --> 01:03:09,983
- Let's only be a big,
giant baby, (crying)

1415
01:03:09,983 --> 01:03:11,518
- Oh, let me go!

1416
01:03:11,518 --> 01:03:14,003
- I just wanna help you die
with a modicum of dignity!

1417
01:03:14,003 --> 01:03:16,509
- When you die you don't suffer any more!

1418
01:03:16,509 --> 01:03:18,717
You don't have a master!

1419
01:03:18,717 --> 01:03:20,179
- You must fight back, brother!

1420
01:03:20,179 --> 01:03:22,846
For you, for me, for Jane!

1421
01:03:22,846 --> 01:03:25,053
As for all who want to live free!

1422
01:03:25,053 --> 01:03:26,590
Listen to me.

1423
01:03:26,590 --> 01:03:27,837
Perhaps there is a way.

1424
01:03:27,837 --> 01:03:29,949
Only ten minutes but you can do it.

1425
01:03:29,949 --> 01:03:31,975
Go to a deep sleep, a false death!

1426
01:03:31,975 --> 01:03:33,917
Ten minutes with no life.

1427
01:03:33,917 --> 01:03:35,645
It is in your power.

1428
01:03:35,645 --> 01:03:39,217
- Well, I'm just sore, is all.

1429
01:03:39,217 --> 01:03:42,023
- Kobras does not know it.

1430
01:03:42,023 --> 01:03:43,580
He cannot take it from you.

1431
01:03:43,580 --> 01:03:46,018
- Please get off, I'm
feeling funny "down there."

1432
01:03:46,018 --> 01:03:47,437
- Hold your breath.

1433
01:03:47,437 --> 01:03:49,922
Your heartbeat can slow down.

1434
01:03:49,922 --> 01:03:53,730
- I just have to not wiggle.

1435
01:03:53,730 --> 01:03:55,608
- Diminish.

1436
01:03:55,608 --> 01:03:56,845
- I mean, anybody would feel this, right?

1437
01:03:56,845 --> 01:04:00,322
It's natural, right?

1438
01:04:00,322 --> 01:04:01,996
- Stop.

1439
01:04:01,996 --> 01:04:06,434
- So pumas are suicidally
depressive mouth-breathers?

1440
01:04:06,434 --> 01:04:09,868
- We show you now the general
vicinity of the heart.

1441
01:04:09,868 --> 01:04:11,980
- That is right, Tony.

1442
01:04:11,980 --> 01:04:13,378
Let yourself go.

1443
01:04:13,378 --> 01:04:14,508
- Stop working out.

1444
01:04:14,508 --> 01:04:19,508
- You are dead, you are dead
for all, even for Kobras.

1445
01:04:20,596 --> 01:04:23,498
(quiet music)

1446
01:04:23,498 --> 01:04:28,498
- Duhhhhhhh, okay.

1447
01:04:32,531 --> 01:04:37,531
(doors clanging)

1448
01:04:44,819 --> 01:04:46,376
- Hey, look what we made, Mike.

1449
01:04:46,376 --> 01:04:48,072
- Why that looks like a--

1450
01:04:48,072 --> 01:04:49,758
why that looks for all
the world like a replica

1451
01:04:49,758 --> 01:04:51,506
of the head of Roger Whittaker.

1452
01:04:51,506 --> 01:04:53,972
- We made it with our genuine Aztec mask.

1453
01:04:53,972 --> 01:04:55,389
- Wow, that's great.

1454
01:04:55,389 --> 01:04:56,725
You know, I can hear him sing right now.

1455
01:04:56,725 --> 01:05:00,479
♫ I left my ship out in the harbor ♫

1456
01:05:00,479 --> 01:05:02,526
I assume you gained control
of his mind and his will.

1457
01:05:02,526 --> 01:05:04,639
- There's no other reason I
can think of to own a replica

1458
01:05:04,639 --> 01:05:06,431
of the head of Roger Whittaker.

1459
01:05:06,431 --> 01:05:07,241
- Yeah, exactly.

1460
01:05:07,241 --> 01:05:08,468
- But I have to ask why.

1461
01:05:08,468 --> 01:05:09,471
Why Roger Whittaker?

1462
01:05:09,471 --> 01:05:11,283
Why not, say, Barbara Feldon?
- Feldon?

1463
01:05:11,283 --> 01:05:12,862
Right, we thought of that, okay, Mike?

1464
01:05:12,862 --> 01:05:15,689
And Sting and Chipmunk
and Senator John Warner.

1465
01:05:15,689 --> 01:05:17,940
- And Puff Daddy and Al
Checchi and Webb Pierce

1466
01:05:17,940 --> 01:05:20,168
and Judy Carne and Joan Sutherland.

1467
01:05:20,168 --> 01:05:21,704
- And George Lindsay and Barbara Bush.

1468
01:05:21,704 --> 01:05:22,557
- And people like that.

1469
01:05:22,557 --> 01:05:24,169
And Mike, when you only
have time to effectively

1470
01:05:24,169 --> 01:05:25,415
control one person--

1471
01:05:25,415 --> 01:05:26,600
- We have other things to do, Mike.

1472
01:05:26,600 --> 01:05:28,510
- Then Roger Whittaker
is the perfect choice.

1473
01:05:28,510 --> 01:05:29,896
Take our word for it.

1474
01:05:29,896 --> 01:05:32,690
It's who we got, now what
do you wanna do with him?

1475
01:05:32,690 --> 01:05:35,933
- Well, I can't think of anything at all.

1476
01:05:35,933 --> 01:05:38,215
- Use your imagination, man!

1477
01:05:38,215 --> 01:05:39,858
It's Roger Whittaker!

1478
01:05:39,858 --> 01:05:42,535
That means songs, sure, but he
can probably do other things,

1479
01:05:42,535 --> 01:05:44,652
you know, light typing and filing.

1480
01:05:44,652 --> 01:05:46,315
And maybe you need help
with your hand-washing.

1481
01:05:46,315 --> 01:05:47,691
- No, no I don't.

1482
01:05:47,691 --> 01:05:49,291
Frankly, I think it's a waste of time.

1483
01:05:49,291 --> 01:05:50,497
- Oh, fine, we go to all this trouble,

1484
01:05:50,497 --> 01:05:53,792
hand Mike Roger Whittaker,
and he drops the ball.

1485
01:05:53,792 --> 01:05:55,308
- Here's what we all-- here's Mike,

1486
01:05:55,308 --> 01:05:58,169
"Duhhh, what do I do with this?"

1487
01:05:58,169 --> 01:06:00,559
You can just go on with your
Roger Whittaker-free life,

1488
01:06:00,559 --> 01:06:02,372
you poor sap, but the
next time you need to hear

1489
01:06:02,372 --> 01:06:04,804
"Durham Town," you're
on your own, good luck!

1490
01:06:04,804 --> 01:06:06,990
- Remember, though, we
control Roger Whittaker.

1491
01:06:06,990 --> 01:06:07,705
- That's right.

1492
01:06:07,705 --> 01:06:08,473
- So watch your back!

1493
01:06:08,473 --> 01:06:10,126
Roger Whittaker could
be on you at any moment.

1494
01:06:10,126 --> 01:06:11,180
- There he is!
- Woahh!

1495
01:06:11,180 --> 01:06:14,017
- I'm kidding, this time.

1496
01:06:14,017 --> 01:06:15,617
- Yeah, look at him run!

1497
01:06:15,617 --> 01:06:17,121
We'll be right back, everybody.

1498
01:06:17,121 --> 01:06:21,141
In the meantime be on the
lookout for Roger Whittaker.

1499
01:06:21,141 --> 01:06:25,525
(sinister lauging)

1500
01:06:25,525 --> 01:06:30,525
(theme music)

1501
01:06:32,918 --> 01:06:35,327
- There he is, Roger Whittaker!

1502
01:06:35,327 --> 01:06:37,099
- I'm scared.

1503
01:06:37,099 --> 01:06:42,099
- Oh, I overdid it on the Fancy Feast.

1504
01:06:42,460 --> 01:06:47,205
- Later, Ma Barker and the
gang come to finish him off.

1505
01:06:47,205 --> 01:06:50,713
Tee-hee, tee-hee.

1506
01:06:50,713 --> 01:06:55,713
- They're here and the
cupcakes are still in the oven!

1507
01:06:56,100 --> 01:07:00,122
- Friends are visiting for MURDER!

1508
01:07:00,122 --> 01:07:02,063
(doors slam)

1509
01:07:02,063 --> 01:07:06,990
- Pumaman!

1510
01:07:06,990 --> 01:07:11,864
- It's Cliff Claven! Hey, Cliffy!

1511
01:07:11,864 --> 01:07:13,347
- So let's cut his ears and paws off,

1512
01:07:13,347 --> 01:07:16,653
we get the fifty buck bounty.

1513
01:07:16,653 --> 01:07:21,250
- So tense right here.

1514
01:07:21,250 --> 01:07:23,074
- Tee-hee, tee-hee.

1515
01:07:23,074 --> 01:07:25,870
- Shh!
- Tee-hee.

1516
01:07:25,870 --> 01:07:30,870
- Tell Santa I love him.

1517
01:07:33,327 --> 01:07:37,241
- He won't get my Amontillado.

1518
01:07:37,241 --> 01:07:38,244
- He's had it.

1519
01:07:38,244 --> 01:07:39,108
- Chicken pox.

1520
01:07:39,108 --> 01:07:42,627
You won't catch it from us.

1521
01:07:42,627 --> 01:07:44,717
- So anyway, do you have a new modem?

1522
01:07:44,717 --> 01:07:45,934
- We found him.

1523
01:07:45,934 --> 01:07:47,693
He's committed suicide.

1524
01:07:47,693 --> 01:07:49,923
Shall I put a bullet in
him, just to be sure.

1525
01:07:49,923 --> 01:07:51,522
- No, that would be cheating.

1526
01:07:51,522 --> 01:07:55,661
- No, it has to look like
an unfortunate accident.

1527
01:07:55,661 --> 01:07:58,327
But be sure that he's dead.

1528
01:07:58,327 --> 01:07:59,725
